```
Reds: `summary`

## Controls

- `control: pg resolves to the fake, and a clean run is summarised at INFO as complete`

## THE CELLS — state it to yourself before you write a line

At the untouched tip all three cells pass: pg resolves to the fake; two clean tenants give `[INFO] ... Tenant DB migrations complete {"migrated":2,"failed":0,"skipped":0,"total":2}`; one clean tenant plus `qa_ghost` give `[WARN] ... Tenant DB migrations INCOMPLETE — 1 tenant(s) FAILED {"migrated":1,"failed":1,...}`; `qa_two_errors` fails every statement and its FAILED line carries `"error":"qa statement 1 refused"`. Under FIRSTERRORLAST the error becomes the last statement's (`qa statement 39 refused`), so `firsterr` fails by assertion; the summaries do not move. Under SUMMARYINFO the failed run's summary starts `[INFO]`, and under SUMMARYCOMPLETE it says `complete`, so `summary` fails by assertion in both; the counts JSON is unchanged (which is why ks1125 cannot see either). The control passes under every tamper: a clean run is `[INFO] ... complete` in all three.

**MEASURED, not predicted** (`--shared` scratch clone at `59412d057`, the harness's `prepare_clone.sh` farm, the service's own `npx vitest run`): see `## Measurements` below.

